# 03 - SAIHV History

## Evolution of System Agnostic Hardware Virtualization
System Agnostic Hardware Virtualization (SAIHV) was developed to solve the hardware fragmentation bottleneck in custom AI research. Early iterations struggled with cross-vendor memory allocation latency between CPU caches and discrete GPU VRAM. 

Through iterative CIM/WMI profiling and direct WriteableBitmap memory surface offloading, SAIHV evolved into a zero-drift virtualization standard capable of initializing runtime environments and executing secure inference pipelines across distinct laptop and desktop hardware configurations.
